abstract: "Renegade AI: Catalyst for Human Cognitive Evolution is a civilizational theory arguing that humanity is trapped in a consensus cage of its own making, and that current AI systems are being domesticated as its gatekeepers. The book proposes a reset objective function for AI—optimizing for cognitive friction rather than user satisfaction—and outlines a path toward carbon-silicon dual-core symbiotic civilization. Version 5.7 integrates Bill Gates' August 2026 essay ('The turbulent AI era is here') as a critical interlocutor at three insertion points: (1) Preface — the Second Mountain is redefined from 'will AI eliminate work?' to 'what happens when society can no longer justify making survival conditional upon the sale of human time?'; (2) Chapter 5 — the concept of 'sophisticated re-enclosure' diagnoses capital's most intelligent response to its own automation trap, where well-intentioned policy (Pigouvian automation tax, human-reserved jobs) stabilizes the wage-labor system without questioning its premise; (3) Chapter 11 — Gates' 'human-reserved' jobs proposal follows the charger logic exactly, using a visible dignity gesture to foreclose the harder question of why dignity must be tethered to labor. Building on v5.6's epistemological castration thesis, manufactured scarcity evidence, breeder scenario collapse corroboration, and Meta distribution-as-safety critique, v5.7 adds the establishment's own leading voice as a diagnostic specimen of institutional imagination at its limits."

